    <string name="about_app">About BenSuet Stay</string>
    <string name="about_body">BenSuet Stay helps South African students find safe, verified accommodation near their campus, with NSFAS and self-funded options in one place. Built by Mansuet Dev.</string>
    <string name="osm_attribution">Distances use location data © OpenStreetMap contributors (Nominatim).</string>
    <string name="delete_account">Delete my account</string>
    <string name="delete_account_subtitle">Permanently remove your profile and sign-in</string>
    <string name="delete_account_confirm_title">Delete your account?</string>
    <string name="delete_account_confirm_body">This permanently deletes your BenSuet Stay profile and sign-in. This can\'t be undone.</string>
    <string name="account_deleted">Your account has been deleted.</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_body">BenSuet Stay only collects what it needs to connect students with accommodation.\n\nWhat we collect: your name, email, home address, institution and funding type. When you apply for a room we also store your SA ID number, student number, campus, next-of-kin details and the names of the documents you chose. For landlords: name, email and phone number.\n\nWhy: to show suitable residences, to let landlords process your viewings and applications, and to send you updates about them.\n\nWho can see it: only you, the landlord of the residence you contact, and BenSuet Stay administrators. Our database security rules enforce this.\n\nWhere it is stored: Google Firebase (Cloud Firestore, Johannesburg region). Passwords are handled by Firebase Authentication and are never stored by the app.\n\nYour rights under POPIA: you can view and update your details in Settings, and delete your account at any time under Settings → Privacy → Delete my account. For anything else, use Settings → Help → Contact support.</string>
    <string name="faq_s_q1">How do I book a viewing?</string>
    <string name="faq_s_a1">Open a listing and tap Book Viewing, then choose a date and time. The landlord confirms or declines it, and you get a notification either way.</string>
    <string name="faq_s_q2">How do I apply for a room?</string>
    <string name="faq_s_a2">Open a listing, choose a room type and tap Select a room. NSFAS students confirm their NSFAS details; self-funded students add next-of-kin details and their documents. Track it under Settings → My Applications.</string>
    <string name="faq_s_q3">Can I use the app without internet?</string>
    <string name="faq_s_a3">Yes. Listings you have already opened stay visible, and viewing requests or applications made offline are saved on your phone and sent automatically when you reconnect.</string>
    <string name="faq_s_q4">Why don\'t I see every residence?</string>
    <string name="faq_s_a4">The homepage starts with your funding type and Near my campus turned on. Tap All or Near my campus to widen the search, or change these defaults in Settings → Home screen.</string>
    <string name="faq_l_q1">Who creates and edits my listings?</string>
    <string name="faq_l_a1">The BenSuet Stay admin team creates listings and assigns them to you. To change a listing or your own details, use Contact support, or Request a change under Personal Information.</string>
    <string name="faq_l_q2">How do I handle viewing requests?</string>
    <string name="faq_l_a2">Open Bookings and confirm or decline each request. When you decline, give a reason and suggest another time. The student is notified straight away.</string>
    <string name="faq_l_q3">What happens when I approve an application?</string>
    <string name="faq_l_a3">One space is taken off that room type automatically, and the student sees your note under My Applications.</string>
